The bug occurs because the code relies on the file position of the `.text` section in the debug file, which can be empty or have different alignments and positions compared to the mmap-ed binary. This leads to incorrect symbol resolution when the debug file is stripped of non-debug sections or has reordered sections, resulting in an inaccurate computation of `text_offset`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
for (i = 0; i < symbols_count; ++i) {
    if (!strcmp(bfd_asymbol_name(symbols[i]), "__ImageBase") ||
        !strcmp(bfd_asymbol_name(symbols[i]), "__image_base__"))
        break;
}
if (i < symbols_count) {
    dso->text_offset = section->vma - (u32)section->vma;
    dso->text_offset += (u32)bfd_asymbol_value(symbols[i]);
}
```
Reason:
The fix involves searching for the `__ImageBase` symbol in the loaded symbols and using its value to compute the `text_offset`. This approach correctly accounts for the image base in the PE file format, ensuring accurate symbol resolution even when the `.text` section's file position is unreliable or when sections are reordered.

